  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Frost/freeze conditions expected late tonight \nand early Tuesday morning over portions of the western and \ncentral Alleghenies \n\nUpgraded freeze watch to warning for McKean, Potter, Elk, and\nCameron counties earlier this aft. \n\nLight winds, clear skies, and low PW values and low dewpoints \nwill result in a chilly night, with the potential for frost and \neven a freeze in a few spots across the northwestern mountains.\n\nTemperatures should moderate during the day, as the area of \nhigh pressure shifts to the east.\n\nMore information below.\n\nPlacement of sfc high becomes somewhat less favorable for \nfrost/freeze Tuesday night as it migrates eastward to the Mid \nAtlantic coast by 12Z Wed. \n\n-------------------------------------------------------------\n \nKEY MESSAGE 2: Extended stretch of dry and seasonable Fall \nweather this week\n\nHigh confidence in a prolonged stretch of dry and seasonable \nFall wx this week with cool nights and refreshing afternoons\nwith low humidity. The next chance of rain is on Sunday.\n\nThis will give the area a much needed chance to dry out from\nthe wet summer and early fall so far.",
